WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.320
Let’s talk about a 
mountain territory 

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.640
that people are killing 
each other over.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.640
It’s called Nagorno-Karabakh. 

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.280
And the fight’s between Armenia and Azerbaijan.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.040
Soldiers and civilians 
are being killed.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.520
So why are they fighting? 

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:35.280
How long has it been
 going on for?

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.880
And why are countries like Turkey involved?

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.920
The first shots were 
fired in July

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.120
before all-out war broke out at the end of September.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:55.400
It’s been the worst fighting there in 25 years.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.680
But the grievances 
go back generations.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:58.200
But the grievances 
go back generations.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.520
At the heart of the 
dispute is a region called

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.040
Nagorno-Karabakh.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.000
And here it is in a crowded neighbourhood 

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.840
known as the 
South Caucasus.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.640
Nagorno-Karabakh 
lies entirely 

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.520
within Azerbaijan’s
borders.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.680
It’s internationally recognised as being part of the country. 

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.840
Full stop.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.840
Here’s the thing. 

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.040
It’s controlled by
ethnic Armenians  

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.720
backed by Armenia.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.360
And surrounding Nagorno-Karabakh

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.920
are lands that 
Armenia controls.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.480
Then you’ve got all 
the big neighbours. 

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.520
Like Iran which 
borders both.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.640
Turkey — it’s long been
 an ally of Azerbaijan.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.640
And then there’s Russia.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.120
It supplies weapons to both Armenia and Azerbaijan.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:38.360
We’ll get into all the geopolitics later 

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.960
but first here’s what Nagorno-Karabakh looks like.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.880
It makes up 5% of 
Azeri territory.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.200
But almost twice that 
much land around it

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.520
is controlled by 
Armenian forces.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.520
About 150,000 
people live here. 

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.440
It holds its own elections 
and governs itself.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:02.400
But right now 
it’s a warzone.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.320
Many people are living 
in their basements  

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.760
because of the shelling.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.520
And local officials say half the people who live there 

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.600
have been 
forced to leave.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:15.440
The thing about this region is that it’s been fought over 

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.080
for a long time.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.240
Iran had control in the mid-18th century. 

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.840
Then the Russians 
took over.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.160
The British and the Ottomans were in there too.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.680
But a key date in all 
of this is 1920.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.400
That’s when Armenia and Azerbaijan went to war 

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.640
over Nagorno-Karabakh and Azerbaijan, backed by Russia

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.920
got control.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.440
A year later it was promised 
to the Armenians 

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.800
but Stalin turned around and made sure Azerbaijan 

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.320
held on to it.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:44.440
By 1988 the Soviet Union
 was crumbling.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:46.440
And the Armenians in Nagorno-Karabakh

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.280
took advantage of 
the power vacuum 

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:50.440
and voted to 
join Armenia.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:54.280
So when the Soviet Union finally fell apart in 1991

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.520
so did whatever was left of peace in the South Caucasus.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.680
1992 was when the fighting really intensified

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.760
right after Armenians in Nagorno-Karabakh 

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.640
declared independence.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.640
Both sides accuse each 
other of atrocities.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.200
Tens of thousands of local Azeris and Armenians 

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.200
were killed

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.640
A million people had 
to leave their homes.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.400
In the end the Armenians pushed Azerbaijan’s forces 

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.880
out of Nagorno-Karabakh, seized territories around it

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.400
and it all finally ended 
in a ceasefire in 1994.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:42.720
That ceasefire 
has been ignored

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.960
by both Armenia and Azerbaijan over the years.
 

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.080
And the sense of injustice over what happened in that war 

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.200
the killings and mass displacement

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.200
hasn’t gone away.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:12.320
And now both sides are tapping into that anger.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:15.200
It’s full-scale war 
all over again: 

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.720
trenches

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:19.720
tanks

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.480
air attacks.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:34.040
Azeri forces have been attacking Nagorno-Karabakh’s  

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.040
main city Stepanakert.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.320
Armenian men there have been signing up to fight back.

00:04:44.520 --> 00:04:47.640
Exact numbers are next to impossible to come by 

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:54.240
but soldiers and civilians on both sides have been killed.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.440
Armenian forces have been attacking Azerbaijan too. 

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:02.520
The border city of Ganja has been among the hardest hit.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.520
So how and why did the fighting start up again?

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.600
The answer depends entirely on who you ask.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.440
Armenia says Azerbaijan attacked first.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.680
Azerbaijan says it acted
 in self-defence.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.200
What’s clear is that it’s not exactly an even fight.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:33.320
Our colleagues at AJ Labs put together these infographics

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:36.080
to show just how much 
more Azerbaijan spends  

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.360
on its military, how many more soldiers it has

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.920
and how much 
more artillery.

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:51.120
And the Azeris have been showing it off.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.200
This is an actual music video released by the Azeri military. 

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.520
The Armenians are rallying their people too.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.120
But what’s making this particular fight different     

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.880
from all the other 
skirmishes is that 

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:07.840
other countries are getting involved in a big way.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.840
Part of Turkey’s connection to Azerbaijan is cultural.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.520
The Azeris are a Turkic-speaking people.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.880
It’s got the Armenians in Nagorno-Karabakh

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.720
looking for outside help too.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.880
So how involved is Turkey in the actual fighting?

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.960
Well that’s difficult 
to pin down.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.760
Azerbaijan’s using military drones supplied by  

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:14.240
Turkey and Israel.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.920
And Turkey’s accused of recruiting Syrian fighters

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.520
to help against the 
Armenians

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.040
which Turkey and 
Azerbaijan flatly deny.

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.400
So what’s in it for Turkey 
and Azerbaijan?

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.840
Beyond trying to get back what they see as Azeri land? 

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.120
Well something to consider 
is that this region 

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:43.200
is rich in oil and gas.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:45.800
Pipelines snake across 
the region. 

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:49.440
Oil and gas make up 90% of Azerbaijan’s exports.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.720
And as for Turkey, Azerbaijan is now its biggest supplier 

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:54.000
of natural gas.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.480
So understandably any instability here 

00:07:56.480 --> 00:07:59.080
is bad for business 
all around.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.400
Azerbaijan accuses the Armenians of attacking  

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:04.760
a major oil pipeline which Armenia denies.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.920
One thing’s for sure. 

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.600
Azerbaijan’s oil-and-gas has come in handy.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.640
The other reason Turkey and Azerbaijan say they support  

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.960
the offensive on Nagorno-Karabakh 

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.800
is that they think the dispute has been allowed to fester.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:27.600
And now is the time to resolve it once and for all.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.000
It’s true that over the 
years there’ve been 

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.640
lots of negotiations.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.560
The UN’s put out a 
bunch of resolutions

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.880
to stop the fighting.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.880
And all the big international organisations

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.120
have weighed in too, including something called  

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:54.040
the Minsk Group led by Russia, France and the United States.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.360
They came close to getting the two sides to agree on

00:08:56.360 --> 00:08:59.600
a peace plan in 2007 
but it fell apart.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.720
But like all the other 
plans so far

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:10.800
they’ve failed to overcome that deep mistrust.

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.440
Both sides accuse each other of terrible things: 

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:57.760
massacres, ethnic cleansing and taking land  

00:09:57.760 --> 00:09:59.640
so it’s hard to make peace.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.800
Ceasefires only 
pause the fighting

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.120
they don’t resolve it — and history has shown that.

